;; gates.edn — fleet-ci の gate matrix（tick.cljs の唯一の対象リスト）。
;;
;; ADR-2607178000 の runner は対象 14 repo とノード（zebulun/asher）を
;; スクリプト内にハードコードしていた。ここを data にして「1行足せば対象が増える」
;; 状態にする（ノードは指定しない — 実行先は nodes.edn の capability から
;; tick.cljs が選ぶ）。
;;
;; :gate kinds
;;   :jvm-test   deps.edn の :test alias（cognitect test-runner）を clojure -M:test で回す
;;               → node cap :jvm 必須
;;   :nbb-test   nbb のテストエントリを回す（:classpath / :entry）
;;               → node cap :node 必須
;;   :nbb-script gates/ 配下の nbb script をノードに配って repo tree に対して回す
;;               → node cap :node 必須
;;               :cap を明記した場合はその capability を要求する（例 :zig）
;;
;; 配送（ノードに何を置くか）
;;   既定             mirror からの `git archive` tarball（`.git` は入らない）
;;   :include-ext     その拡張子だけを詰めた tarball（`:min-files` が床）
;;   :ship-self-bundle true
;;                    mirror からの **git bundle**。ノードで git init → fetch →
;;                    checkout -f → sha 照合して**履歴つきの本物の checkout** を作る。
;;                    **repo 自身の git 履歴を読む gate だけが指定する**（ADR-2608134200）。
;;                    `:include-ext` / `:min-files` とは併用できない（bundle は tree の
;;                    部分集合ではないので filter が効かず、書いても no-op になるため
;;                    `gate-input!` が拒否する）。full history を毎回送るので、
;;                    大きい repo では 200MB の天井に当たる。
;;
;; org は west.yml の remote から解決するのでここには書かない（drift 防止）。
{:policy "fleet-ci/tip-verify/v1"
 :gate-timeout-ms 1800000            ;; 1 gate 30 分（clojure の初回 maven 解決を含む）
 :status-context-prefix "fleet-ci/murakumo"
 ;; receipt を署名する弱権限鍵（kagi item 名）。fleet-keys.edn には**入っていない** —
 ;; pin 前進も governance quorum も持たない（漏れても append-only の fleet-ci.edn に
 ;; 偽の行を足せるだけ）。machine ごとに別 identity を enroll する運用なので、
 ;; 鍵を machine 間でコピーしない（ADR-2607178000 の murakumo-ci は別マシンの identity）。
 ;; 2026-07-30: `fleet-agent-murakumo-ci-tip` は fleet-agents.edn に enroll 済み
 ;; （公開鍵 2aa25c7c、DID z6MkhKgm…）だが、**秘密鍵がこのマシンの kagi にも
 ;; PEM にも無い** — 狙い撃ちで両 compartment を確認して不在、vault 自体は
 ;; unlock 可能（lock 障害ではない）。そのため tick は gate を 1 本も実行できず
 ;; `no such item` で死んでいた。
 ;;
 ;; そこで **このマシン専用の identity を新規 enroll した**（README の
 ;; 「machine ごとに別 identity」に従う）。既存 `-tip` の鍵を推測で作り直すと
 ;; enroll 済み公開鍵と一致せず receipt の検証が壊れるので、名前を分ける。
 ;; 秘密鍵は kagi と ~/.gftd/fleet-ci-signer-tip.pem（mode 600、plist が期待
 ;; する路 = ADR-2607178000 §3 が認めた launchd 経路）の両方に置いた。
 :signer-kagi "fleet-agent-murakumo-ci-tip-25mbair"
 :landing {:repo "com-junkawasaki/root"
           :branch "main"
           :receipts "manifest/fleet-ci.edn"
           :west "manifest/west.yml"
           :db "manifest/fleet-db.edn"}
 ;; Radicle 反映。**落ちたときだけ issue を開く**（rad 1.9.1 に commit status に
 ;; 当たる COB は無い — job も ci も status も無く、書ける面は issue か patch の
 ;; コメント/レビューだけ。patch は tip 駆動のこの CI には存在しない）。
 ;;
 ;; 実行先が seed node なのは、gad が systemd で node 常駐・gate 対象を seed
 ;; 済みで、announce できる identity がそちらにあるため。この laptop の node は
 ;; 停止したままで、その鍵の passphrase item（radicle-node-passphrase）は今も
 ;; kagi に無い。
 ;;
 ;; :passphrase-item — COB の署名鍵を unlock する passphrase の kagi item
 ;; （compartment personal）。gad に ssh-agent は無いので、これが唯一の unlock
 ;; 手段。2026-07-26 に実際に置いた（ADR-2607252200 はこの置き場所を決めて
 ;; いたが、実測では `no such item` のままだった＝実行されていなかった）。
 ;; 値は stdin 経由でのみ渡す（argv はリモートの ps に出る）。
 ;;
 ;; RID は manifest/repos.edn の rad-rids から orgs/<org>/<repo> で引く。RID の
 ;; 無い repo は skip して名前を出す（黙って落とさない）。
 :rad {:enabled true
       :host "gad"
       :bin "/home/gad/.radicle/bin/rad"
       :run-as "gad"
       :passphrase-item "radicle-seed-gad-passphrase"}
 ;; CD: gate が green かつ west pin が tip より遅れているとき pin を前進させる。
 ;; 対象は :cd true の repo のみ（opt-in — 静かな pin 前進を全 repo に広げない）。
 :cd {:pin-advance-on-green true}
 :repos
 ;; ── :jvm-test → :nbb-test, only where the ClojureScript run was MEASURED to
 ;;    be the same run (ADR-2608170200) ──────────────────────────────────────
 ;;
 ;; `:jvm-test` needs node cap :jvm, which `nodes.edn` puts on 2 of 10 hosts
 ;; (4 slots) against 56 :jvm-test entries; `:node` is on 4 (8 slots), and
 ;; placement.cljs costs them 600s vs 180s. So moving a gate off the JVM is
 ;; worth real queue time — which is exactly why it must not be done on the
 ;; strength of "the sources are .cljc".
 ;;
 ;; The trap, measured 2026-08-17 on columnar: `test/run.cljs` required one of
 ;; the suite's three test namespaces, so nbb ran 10 of 36 tests and printed
 ;; `Ran 10 tests ... 0 failures`. With group/group deliberately broken, the
 ;; partial runner still exited 0. Flipping that gate would have moved it to a
 ;; cheaper node AND silently dropped two thirds of the suite, and the receipt
 ;; would have looked the same. (Fixed upstream in columnar 5e165f0 before the
 ;; flip below.)
 ;;
 ;; Admission for a flip is therefore four measurements, not one:
 ;;   1. `Ran N tests containing M assertions` is IDENTICAL under
 ;;      `clojure -M:test` and under `nbb --classpath <cp> <entry>`.
 ;;   2. The nbb entry exits non-zero with the subject broken and zero with it
 ;;      intact -- and the reported failure is the thing that was broken.
 ;;   3. deps.edn has no cross-repo dep the test path needs: the gate ships one
 ;;      repo's tree, so `:nbb-test`'s classpath cannot reach a sibling.
 ;;   4. The runner covers the whole suite:
 ;;        nbb --classpath ".:scripts/nbb_compat" \
 ;;          scripts/verify-cljs-runner-completeness.cljs --repo orgs/<org>/<name>
 ;;      reports it complete. Condition 1 catches this today only because someone
 ;;      thought to run both sides and compare; the detector is what makes it hold
 ;;      after the flip, when nothing runs `clojure -M:test` any more and there is
 ;;      no second number to compare against. Measured 2026-08-17: 22 of the 201
 ;;      repos with a ClojureScript runner do not pass it.
 ;;
 ;; Measured, all three, on the three flipped below:
 ;;   kagami        19 tests / 121 assertions  JVM == nbb;  broken -> exit 1
 ;;   columnar      36 tests / 117 assertions  JVM == nbb;  broken -> exit 1
 ;;   org-ietf-csv  10 tests /  38 assertions  JVM == nbb;  broken -> exit 1
 ;;
 ;; NOT flipped, with the reason, so the next reader does not re-derive it:
 ;;   kotobase-storage  test/run.cljs is a COMPLEMENT, not a port -- it covers
 ;;                     the async/Worker path the JVM suite cannot reach, and
 ;;                     prints no `Ran N tests` line at all (the gate's own
 ;;                     floor, exit 93, would reject it). Both halves are real
 ;;                     coverage; dropping either loses tests.
 ;;   org-ietf-cbor     its cljs half is `shadow-cljs compile` -- a JVM build.
 ;;                     No nbb entry exists yet.
 ;;   io-multiformats   NOT flipped, and it does not need to be: it has TWO
 ;;                     entries now, `:jvm-test` here and the
 ;;                     `nbb-cross-runtime-multiformats` one below.
 ;;                     That repo has one defect per host, measured 2026-08-17:
 ;;                       reverting `core/varint` to shifts  -> 3 red on CLJS, 0 on JVM
 ;;                       removing read-varint's mult cap    -> 2 red on JVM,  0 on CLJS
 ;;                     so flipping would have traded one half for the other.
 ;;
 ;;                     ⚠ An earlier version of this note said two gates for
 ;;                     one repo were impossible here -- "entries are keyed by
 ;;                     :name and the status context derives from it, so a
 ;;                     second entry would collide". **That was wrong, and it
 ;;                     was wrong about a file that already contained the
 ;;                     counterexample**: `io-ipld` has had two entries since
 ;;                     ADR-2608060500, disambiguated by `:id`. Read the file
 ;;                     before reporting what it cannot do.
 ;;   chain, io-ipld, io-ipld-car, nekko, org-apache-avro, kotobase-lake,
 ;;   tech-ipfs-specs-ipns, sakkyokuka
 ;;                     zero .clj files, but their test path needs sibling
 ;;                     repos through deps.edn (condition 3). The note at
 ;;                     "ongaku" below records the same constraint.
 [{:name "kagami" :gate :nbb-test :classpath "src:test" :entry "run-tests.cljs" :cd true}
  {:name "nekko" :gate :jvm-test :cd true}
  {:name "bonsai" :gate :jvm-test :cd true}
  {:name "langgraph" :gate :jvm-test :cd true}
  {:name "kagitaba" :gate :jvm-test :cd true}
  {:name "org-ietf-ed25519" :gate :jvm-test :cd true}
  {:name "org-ietf-cbor" :gate :jvm-test :cd true}
  {:name "io-multiformats" :gate :jvm-test :cd true}
  {:name "io-ipld" :gate :jvm-test :cd true}
  ;; UnixFS file DAGs. Its fixtures are real kubo CIDs, so this gate answers
  ;; "does `ipfs add` still agree with us" and not "do we agree with
  ;; ourselves" -- the distinction the codec it replaced could not make.
  {:name "tech-ipfs-specs-unixfs" :gate :jvm-test :cd true}
  ;; The filesystem-surface stack (ADR-2608171200). org-ietf-nfs's suite
  ;; starts a real listener and drives it over a socket, so this gate covers
  ;; the three layers composing and not just each codec in isolation.
  {:name "org-ietf-xdr" :gate :jvm-test :cd true}
  {:name "org-ietf-oncrpc" :gate :jvm-test :cd true}
  {:name "org-ietf-nfs" :gate :jvm-test :cd true}
  ;; The physical plane (ADR-2608160100): CARv2 bytes, the storage contract
  ;; that describes where a block lives, and the packed block store over it.
  ;; :jvm-test covers each repo's synchronous suite. What it does NOT cover is
  ;; named here rather than left to be assumed: kotobase-storage-pack's
  ;; Promise driver and its miniflare/R2 end-to-end need npm packages on the
  ;; node, and kotobase-storage-s3's whole suite does (miniflare, shadow-cljs),
  ;; so neither is gated yet.
  {:name "io-ipld-car" :gate :jvm-test :cd true}
  {:name "kotobase-storage" :gate :jvm-test :cd true}
  {:name "kotobase-storage-pack" :gate :jvm-test :cd true}
  ;; kototama cannot take a :jvm-test gate: its :test alias resolves sibling
  ;; :local/root deps that a node never receives, so that gate would fail
  ;; about the classpath forever. The repo declares :test-hermetic for the
  ;; namespaces that need nothing but itself -- linear-journal (at-most-once
  ;; authority consumption, now a content-addressed chain) and execution
  ;; (root ADR-2608160200's execution value and memo decision) -- and this
  ;; gate runs that. :cap :jvm because the script shells to clojure.
  {:name "kototama" :id "kototama-hermetic" :gate :nbb-script :cap :jvm
   :script "gates/kototama-hermetic-test.cljs"
   :include-ext [".edn" ".clj" ".cljc" ".cljs"] :min-files 60 :cd true}
  ;; ---- the accounting plane (ADR-2608171800) --------------------------
  ;;
  ;; Four iterations of work landed here checked only by `clojure -M:test` on
  ;; one workstation. CLAUDE.md's rule is that a gate is not landed until it
  ;; has gone green on the fleet once, and none of these had ever run there.
  ;;
  ;; taxlaw and governor are zero-dependency `.cljc`, so a plain :jvm-test
  ;; is exactly right. governor is the higher-leverage of the two: four
  ;; actors now take their verdict assembly from it, so this gate stands
  ;; between that library and every one of them.
  {:name "governor" :gate :jvm-test :cd true}
  {:name "taxlaw" :gate :jvm-test :cd true}
  ;; These two took their capability library by :local/root until 2026-08-17,
  ;; which made them structurally ungateable -- the fleet ships one repo's
  ;; tree and no siblings, so the classpath could never resolve. Measured
  ;; that day: taxlaw and labor both have ZERO :local/root deps of their own
  ;; and always were git-dep consumable. 4313's deps.edn had said otherwise
  ;; in a comment, about another repo, that nothing ever rechecked.
  {:name "cloud-itonami-isco-4311" :gate :jvm-test :cd true}
  {:name "cloud-itonami-isco-4313" :gate :jvm-test :cd true}
  ;; kintai and tehai, gated the same day and by the same conversion.
  ;;
  ;; The comment that stood here said they could not be, because
  ;; "kotoba-lang/langchain-store is the only library in this plane that
  ;; still carries :local/root deps (two, on langchain-clj)". THAT WAS
  ;; FALSE, and it was false in a way worth recording, because it is the
  ;; identical defect the isco-4313 conversion four commits earlier had just
  ;; fixed: a claim about ANOTHER repository, written in this file, that
  ;; nothing rechecks.
  ;;
  ;; Its origin was a bad measurement. `grep -c local/root deps.edn` counted
  ;; 2 in langchain-store -- both inside COMMENTS explaining that it used to
  ;; be a :local/root and is a git coordinate now (ADR-2608136400). A text
  ;; count was read as a semantic fact. Re-measured by parsing deps.edn as
  ;; EDN and inspecting :deps / :extra-deps / :replace-deps, langchain-store
  ;; has zero, as do psa, shift, worklaw, labor, taxlaw and governor.
  ;;
  ;; There was never a blocker. Both repos were converted (e17e5ea544fb,
  ;; 3870223cbf89) and each verified from a worktree with no sibling
  ;; directory in existence before being listed here.
  {:name "kintai" :gate :jvm-test :cd true}
  {:name "tehai" :gate :jvm-test :cd true}
  {:name "org-ietf-deflate" :gate :jvm-test :cd true}
  {:name "kotobase-block-codec" :gate :jvm-test :cd true}
  {:name "chain" :gate :jvm-test :cd true}
  {:name "org-chainagnostic-cacao" :gate :jvm-test :cd true}
  {:name "tech-ipfs-specs-ipns" :gate :jvm-test :cd true}
  ;; ── protobuf wire, both implementations (ADR-2608170700) ──────────────────
  ;;
  ;; Neither was gated at all. Actions are disabled here (ADR-2607300900), so
  ;; nothing had run dev-protobuf's tests since 2026-08-04 -- and what ran then
  ;; was the JVM half only, while its callers (tech-ipfs-specs-ipns,
  ;; io-libp2p-specs-kad-dht) ship to Workers and browsers. Three defects were
  ;; sitting in that green, all ClojureScript-only: varints past 2^53 decoded
  ;; to silently wrong numbers, fixed64 emitted its low four octets twice, and
  ;; two assertions were host-dependent in the test itself.
  ;;
  ;; dev-protobuf is :nbb-test, and the three admissions at the head of :repos
  ;; were measured 2026-08-17 rather than assumed:
  ;;   1. `Ran 18 tests containing 66 assertions` -- IDENTICAL under
  ;;      `clojure -M:test` and `nbb --classpath src:test test/run.cljs`
  ;;   2. removing the varint guard exits 1 and names the two tests about it;
  ;;      restoring it exits 0
  ;;   3. deps.edn is `{}` -- zero dependencies, so a one-repo tree is enough
  ;; It runs on the cheaper :node capability AND covers the runtime the defects
  ;; lived in, which is the rare case where those point the same way.
  {:name "dev-protobuf" :gate :nbb-test :classpath "src:test" :entry "test/run.cljs" :cd true}
  ;; proto stays :jvm-test, and NOT because nobody checked. Its counts differ
  ;; by runtime -- 13 tests / 89 assertions on the JVM, 11 / 79 under
  ;; `scripts/verify-cljs.cljs` -- because `test/proto/core_test.clj` is
  ;; JVM-only. Admission 1 therefore fails, and picking the nbb entry would
  ;; drop two tests to reach a cheaper node.
  ;; **What this gate does not cover**: the ClojureScript half. That half is
  ;; real (its runner's own docstring is the lesson dev-protobuf lacked --
  ;; "it is tempting to treat a green JVM run as covering both runtimes; it
  ;; does not") and it was green when measured. It is simply not gated, and
  ;; closing that needs a second entry per repo, which this file does not have.
  {:name "proto" :gate :jvm-test :cd true}
  ;; sigv4 signs and VERIFIES the S3 writes this fleet's Workers accept, and
  ;; had no gate of any kind. Probed 2026-08-17 expecting the dev-protobuf
  ;; shape and finding the opposite: `scripts/verify-cljs.cljs` already
  ;; re-runs the load-bearing assertions on nbb -- AWS's two published
  ;; reference signatures, presigning, a non-ASCII round trip, 18 checks --
  ;; and `constant-time-eq?` compares lengths first with the reasoning
  ;; written down. The library was disciplined; nothing was running it.
  ;;
  ;; Verified on judah before landing:
  ;;   intact -> Ran 32 tests / 93 assertions, 0 failures, exit 0
  ;;   `constant-time-eq?`'s length check removed -> exit 1, naming
  ;;   `constant-time-eq-semantics`
  ;;
  ;; The cljs half is covered too, by the second entry below. It was not when
  ;; this was first written: `scripts/verify-cljs.cljs` printed `ok <check>`
  ;; lines rather than a clojure.test summary, which `nbb-cross-runtime.cljs`
  ;; refuses to accept as a pass. That script is now `run-tests.cljs`, a real
  ;; suite, and the old one is deleted rather than kept beside it -- two entry
  ;; points for one parity check is how one of them quietly stops matching.
  {:name "sigv4" :gate :jvm-test :cd true}
  ;; ADR-2608153000 — Valueflows 経済語彙。2026-08-15、実ノードで 1 度緑になった
  ;; ので :cd true に反転（receipt 1d6bd3ca7025、signer did:key:z6MkjyhVmg…）:
  ;;   test-ws-valueflo-algorithms-73816c6-murakumo-judah      Ran 64 tests / 249 assertions
  ;;   test-ws-valueflo-vocabulary-3c89972-murakumo-benjamin   Ran 44 tests / 425 assertions
  ;; algorithms が緑になれるのは deps.edn が sibling を :local/root ではなく
  ;; :git/sha で掴んでいるからで（tick.cljs:729）、log に
  ;; `dep shipped (checkout) io.github.kotoba-lang/ws-valueflo-vocabulary 3c89972
  ;; -> judah` が出ている。:local/root のままなら永久に赤だった。
  ;; ADR-2608153000 — plm は VF の dependent-demand / value-rollup の :mapped 判定の
  ;; 根拠なのに、2026-08-15 まで CI で何も検査していなかった。登録前に
  ;; `--dry-run --only plm` で実ノードに当てて緑を確認した（`:test` alias が
  ;; maven の cognitect test-runner + datomic local を要するので、egress を
  ;; 推測で登録すると恒久的に赤い gate になる）:
  ;;   test-plm-1e0901d-murakumo-judah  exit 0  Ran 31 tests / 118 assertions
  ;; ADR-2608153000 — ENGI。plm と同じ手順で、登録前に `--dry-run --only credits`
  ;; を実ノードに当てて緑を確認した（`:test` alias が maven の cognitect
  ;; test-runner を要し、ws-valueflo-vocabulary の git dep も搬送が要る）:
  ;;   test-credits-909b866-murakumo-judah  exit 0  Ran 70 tests / 432 assertions
  ;;   dep shipped (checkout) io.github.kotoba-lang/ws-valueflo-vocabulary 95e552d -> judah
  {:name "credits" :gate :jvm-test :cd true}
  {:name "plm" :gate :jvm-test :cd true}
  {:name "ws-valueflo-vocabulary" :gate :jvm-test :cd true}
  {:name "ws-valueflo-algorithms" :gate :jvm-test :cd true}

  {:name "kotoba-delta" :gate :nbb-test :classpath "src:test" :entry "run-tests.cljs" :cd true}

  ;; kotoba-selfhost-contracts — the self-host decision slices (ADR-2608110100).
  ;;
  ;; This repo ships COMPILED artifacts (resources/kotoba/selfhost/oracle/*.kir.edn)
  ;; that production loads, and the source they came from (kotoba/*.kotoba). The
  ;; failure that only a gate can catch is drift between the two: editing a
  ;; .kotoba and forgetting `clojure -M:test:gen` leaves production executing the
  ;; OLD decision while every source-compiling test still passes. Locally that
  ;; needs someone to remember; here it does not.
  ;;
  ;; No :include-ext — the tree is small and the drift test READS kotoba/*.kotoba
  ;; off disk. Filtering to .edn would ship the artifacts without their source and
  ;; the gate would fail for the wrong reason (`root-permit-index` is the standing
  ;; example of a gate whose input is not in the tree it is given).
  ;;
  ;; :jvm-test needs the amu closure resolved from git, which needs node egress.
  ;; Measured 2026-08-05: all 10 reachable nodes get 200 from github/maven/npm.
  {:name "kotoba-selfhost-contracts" :gate :jvm-test :cd true}

  ;; inference — the Ollama-compatible surface's decision cores (ADR-2608138800).
  ;;
  ;; Exactly the same drift shape as kotoba-selfhost-contracts above, for the
  ;; same reason: production loads resources/kotodama/oracle/*.kir.edn and the
  ;; source it came from is kotoba/*_core.kotoba. Editing a core and forgetting
  ;; `clojure -M:test:gen` leaves the server executing the OLD decision while
  ;; the semantics tests — which read the shipped artifact — keep passing. That
  ;; specific failure is invisible to every test except the authority check, and
  ;; the authority check only runs if something runs it.
  ;;
  ;; No :include-ext, for the same reason as above: the parity test READS
  ;; kotoba/*_core.kotoba off disk and recompiles it. Filtering to .edn would
  ;; ship the artifacts without their source and the gate would fail for the
  ;; wrong reason.
  ;;
  ;; :jvm-test resolves num/torch/kotoba-kir/amu from git, so the node needs
  ;; outward HTTPS. Do not read that as a property of the fleet — egress is not
  ;; uniform (measured 2026-08-13: one node answered 000 for npm while eight
  ;; answered 200). If this gate starts failing on one node only, measure that
  ;; node before changing the gate.
  {:name "inference" :gate :jvm-test :cd true}

  ;; Kotoba language Q9 Wave 1 / Tranche 1 soak. GitHub Actions is disabled;
  ;; these ten independent repository-local oracle tests are the executable
  ;; evidence consumed by kotoba-lang/scripts/collect-q9-soak.bb. Each tip
  ;; change produces a signed append-only murakumo receipt. Keep :cd false:
  ;; passing the pilot does not authorize consumer cutover or automatic pin
  ;; movement; the Q9 soak gate remains the explicit authority boundary.
  {:name "com-aadhaar" :gate :jvm-test :cd false}
  {:name "com-aave" :gate :jvm-test :cd false}
  {:name "com-abb-robotics" :gate :jvm-test :cd false}
  {:name "com-accela" :gate :jvm-test :cd false}
  {:name "com-accelbyte" :gate :jvm-test :cd false}
  {:name "com-ach-network" :gate :jvm-test :cd false}
  {:name "com-acorrd-standards" :gate :jvm-test :cd false}
  {:name "com-acquia" :gate :jvm-test :cd false}
  {:name "com-adobe" :gate :jvm-test :cd false}
  {:name "com-aftership" :gate :jvm-test :cd false}

  ;; hirameki-patents は**コードではなくデータ**の repo。gate が検査するのは
  ;; 「テストが通るか」ではなく「公開した corpus がバイトと問いの両方で健全か」——
